From f64ee96ed8d69d7f0f4b14ac05699cc33da738dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:39:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 0141: rebuild the HUD overlay .szs in place -- keep the
 original SARC layout

The v2 rebuild re-packed both SARC layers (data_off ~0x12c, files at
4-byte alignment). The originals use data_off 0x2000 (outer) / 0x1000
(inner) and align timg/__Combined.bntx to 0x1000. The repacked .szs made
the CounterCoin layout load with a null sub-object and the game crashed
(SIGSEGV, addr 0x8, main+0x97907c) in a name lookup ~16s after launch.
Rebuild by patching only the .bflyt/.bflan float bytes in place inside the
original SARC; the decompressed SARC now differs from the original in only
the intended float bytes (6/4/1/1/1/3 bytes across the 6 files).
---
 dm/romfs-overlay/LayoutData/CounterCoin.szs   | Bin 19065 -> 43306 bytes
 .../LayoutData/CounterCollectCoin.szs         | Bin 18777 -> 34810 bytes
 dm/romfs-overlay/LayoutData/CounterLife.szs   | Bin 84585 -> 104218 bytes
 dm/romfs-overlay/LayoutData/CounterShine.szs  | Bin 5074 -> 14218 bytes
 dm/romfs-overlay/LayoutData/MapMini.szs       | Bin 12738 -> 29626 bytes
 dm/romfs-overlay/LayoutData/PlayGuide.szs     | Bin 22620 -> 36538 bytes
 6 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

